To ensure thread safety and manage resources properly, the code uses a `try-with-resources` block to create the `ByteArrayInputStream` and `ObjectInputStream`. This ensures that the input stream and object input stream are closed when they are no longer needed. The method also includes a `finally` block to close any input streams that were created but not returned by the method.

The code also includes a call to an external REST API to fetch metadata about the classes being deserialized. This allows the method to verify that the class of each object being deserialized is valid before attempting deserialization. If the class cannot be found, the method throws a `RuntimeException` with a meaningful message.

Finally, the code includes a check to ensure that the byte array contains at least one serialized object. If there are no objects in the input byte array, the method returns `null`.

