The `Game` class initializes the game environment using the configuration settings from the `GameConfig` object passed in its constructor. It has a running flag that determines whether the game loop should continue running. The `run()` method of the `Game` class handles events, updates the game state, and renders the game state on screen. It also limits the frame rate to avoid performance issues.

The `Player`, `Enemy`, and `PowerUp` classes are used to represent the different entities in the game. They have position and velocity attributes that are initialized using the configuration settings from the `GameConfig` object. The `update()` method of each class updates its position and velocity based on the current frame rate and the elapsed time since the last update. The `render()` method of each class renders the entity on screen using the Pygame library.

