This program first checks if the OpenSSL version is at least 1.1.0, and if not, aborts with an error message. Then it sets up a structure to hold the cryptographic primitives and their associated functions, and adds AES-CBC, CAMELLIA-CBC, MD5, SHA1, and RSA-SHA1 using the EVP_add_cipher and EVP_add_digest functions.

To ensure thread safety when adding cryptographic primitives in a multi-threaded environment, the program creates multiple threads to add the primitives concurrently, and uses pthread_join to wait for all threads to complete before continuing with the rest of the program. If any of the threads fail to add the requested primitive, the program attempts to fall back using a fallback mechanism that suggests alternatives based on user preferences.

After adding the cryptographic primitives, the program uses EVP_cleanup to clean up the added primitives after use.

