The class uses a `std::map<std::string, NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU>` to store the RNTIs as keys and the PDUs as values. The map is protected by a mutex to ensure thread safety when adding or retrieving PDUs.

The `addPdu` method takes a `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU` as an argument and adds it to the collection if the RNTI and CRC indication tags are valid. If the input is invalid, the method throws a `std::runtime_error`.

The `getPdu` method takes a string representation of an RNTI as an argument and returns the corresponding PDU if found. If the RNTI is not found, the method throws a `std::runtime_error`.

The `clear` method clears the entire collection.

The `serialize` method serializes the collection into a JSON format by iterating over the map and concatenating the RNTIs and CRC indication values using the `std::ostringstream` class. The resulting string is returned.

