### 2.3.1.3. Detailed Design

The detailed design for this feature will involve several components:

* **NFAPI Provider**: The NFAPI provider will be responsible for providing the CRCFlag to the UE and generating the CRC information.
* **UE**: The UE will be responsible for requesting the CRCFlag from the NFAPI provider, and using it to generate the CRC information.
* **CRC Algorithm**: The CRC algorithm will be used to generate the CRC value of the received data.

The following sequence diagram shows the flow of the data processing in this feature:
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant UE as "UE"
    participant NFAPI_Provider as "NFAPI Provider"
    participant CRC_Algorithm as "CRC Algorithm"
    Note over UE, NFAPI_Provider : Receiving Data from ENODEB
    UE ->> NFAPI_Provider: Request CRCFlag
    NFAPI_Provider -->> UE: CRCFlag(crcflag)
    Note over UE, CRC_Algorithm : Generating CRC Information
    UE ->> CRC_Algorithm: Provide Data to be CRC-ed
    CRC_Algorithm ->> UE: CRC-ed Data and CRC Value
    Note over UE, NFAPI_Provider : Sending CRC Information to ENODEB
    UE ->> NFAPI_Provider: Send CRC-ed Data with CRC Value
```

The following table shows the details of each component in this feature:

| Component | Detailed Design |
| --- | --- |
| NFAPI Provider | Provide CRCFlag to UE and generate CRC information. |
| UE | Request CRCFlag from NFAPI provider, use it to generate CRC information, send CRC-ed data with CRC value to ENODEB. |
| CRC Algorithm | Generate CRC value of received data. |

## 2.3.2. CRC Reception and Verification in UE

This feature involves the ability for a UE to receive and verify the CRC information sent by an ENODEB. The goal is to ensure that the data is not corrupted during transmission.

### 2.3.2.1. Functional Requirements

The following functional requirements will be satisfied by this feature:

* **CRCFlag Received**: A UE will receive the CRCFlag from the NFAPI provider and use it to generate CRC information.
* **CRC Verification**: The UE will verify the CRC value of the received data against the CRC value generated by the ENODEB using the same algorithm. If there is a mismatch, an error indication will be provided to the network.

### 2.3.2.2. User Stories

The following user stories illustrate the functionality provided by this feature:

* **Story 1**: As a UE, I want to receive the CRCFlag from the NFAPI provider so that I can generate CRC information and verify it against the received data.
* **Story 2**: As a UE, I want to be able to verify the CRC value of the received data against the CRC value generated by the ENODEB using the same algorithm, so that I can ensure that the data is not corrupted during transmission.
* **Story 3**: As an ENODEB developer, I want to provide a feature where the UE receives the CRCFlag from the NFAPI provider and generates CRC information, so that the UE can verify the received data against the CRC value generated by the ENODEB using the same algorithm.
* **Story 4**: As an ENODEB developer, I want to provide a feature where the UE verifies the CRC value of the received data against the CRC value generated by the ENODEB using the same algorithm, so that the UE can ensure that the data is not corrupted during transmission.

### 2.3.2.3. Detailed Design

The detailed design for this feature will involve several components:

* **NFAPI Provider**: The NFAPI provider will be responsible for providing the CRCFlag to the UE and generating the CRC information.
* **UE**: The UE will be responsible for requesting the CRCFlag from the NFAPI provider, and using it to generate the CRC information, then verifying the received data against the generated CRC value.
* **CRC Algorithm**: The CRC algorithm will be used to generate the CRC value of the received data.

The following sequence diagram shows the flow of the data processing in this feature:
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant UE as "UE"
    participant NFAPI_Provider as "NFAPI Provider"
    Note over UE, NFAPI_Provider : Receiving Data from ENODEB
    UE ->> NFAPI_Provider: Request CRCFlag
    NFAPI_Provider -->> UE: CRCFlag(crcflag)
    Note over UE, CRC_Algorithm : Generating CRC Information
    UE ->> CRC_Algorithm: Provide Data to be CRC-ed
    CRC_Algorithm ->> UE: CRC-ed Data and CRC Value
    Note over UE, NFAPI_Provider : Sending CRC Information to ENODEB
    UE ->> NFAPI_Provider: Send CRC-ed Data with CRC Value
```

The following table shows the details of each component in this feature:

| Component | Detailed Design |
| --- | --- |
| NFAPI Provider | Provide CRCFlag to UE and generate CRC information. |
| UE | Request CRCFlag from NFAPI provider, use it to generate CRC information, verify received data against generated CRC value using the same algorithm. |
| CRC Algorithm | Generate CRC value of received data. |

## 2.3.3. CRC Error Indication in UE

This feature involves the ability for a UE to indicate an error if the CRC value does not match after verifying it against the generated CRC value. The goal is to ensure that the data is not corrupted during transmission and the UE can detect any errors.

### 2.3.3.1. Functional Requirements

The following functional requirements will be satisfied by this feature:

* **CRC Error Indication**: The UE will indicate an error if the CRC value does not match after verifying it against the generated CRC value.

### 2.3.3.2. User Stories

The following user stories illustrate the functionality provided by this feature:

* **Story 1**: As a UE, I want to indicate an error if the received CRC value does not match the generated CRC value after verifying it using the same algorithm, so that I can detect any errors in the data and ensure that the data is not corrupted during transmission.
* **Story 2**: As an ENODEB developer, I want to provide a feature where the UE indicates an error if the received CRC value does not match the generated CRC value using the same algorithm, so that the network can detect any errors in the data and ensure that the data is not corrupted during transmission.

### 2.3.3.3. Detailed Design

The detailed design for this feature will involve several components:

* **UE**: The UE will be responsible for receiving the CRC value from the ENODEB and verifying it against the generated CRC value using the same algorithm, then indicating an error if there is a mismatch.
* **CRC Algorithm**: The CRC algorithm will be used to generate the CRC value of the received data.

The following sequence diagram shows the flow of the data processing in this feature:
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant UE as "UE"
    participant ENODEB as "ENODEB"
    Note over UE, ENODEB : Receiving Data from ENODEB
    ENODEB ->> UE: Send Data with CRC Value
    Note over UE, CRC_Algorithm : Generating CRC Information
    UE ->> CRC_Algorithm: Provide Data to be CRC-ed
    CRC_Algorithm ->> UE: CRC-ed Data and CRC Value
    Note over UE, ENODEB : Verifying CRC Value
    UE ->> ENODEB: Verify Received CRC Value against Generated CRC Value using the same algorithm
    ENODEB -->> UE: Indicate Error if CRC Values do not Match
```

The following table shows the details of each component in this feature:

| Component | Detailed Design |
| --- | --- |
| UE | Receive data from ENODEB, verify received CRC value against generated CRC value using the same algorithm and indicate an error if there is a mismatch. |
| CRC Algorithm | Generate CRC value of received data. |
| ENODEB | Send data with CRC Value to UE and receive CRC value from UE. Verify received CRC value against generated CRC value using the same algorithm. Indicate error if CRC values do not match. |

public static async Task<T> SendApiRequestAsync<T>(string endpoint, string input, string compressionAlgorithm = "GZIP", string encryptionKey = null, int cacheDurationInSeconds = 300) where T : class {
    // Compress the input data using the specified algorithm
    byte[] compressedData;
    switch (compressionAlgorithm) {
      case "GZIP":
        using (var memoryStream = new MemoryStream()) {
          using (var gzipStream = new GZipStream(memoryStream, CompressionMode.Compress)) {
            var writer = new StreamWriter(gzipStream);
            writer.Write(input);
            writer.Flush();
            compressedData = memoryStream.ToArray();
          }
        }
        break;
      case "Deflate":
        using (var memoryStream = new MemoryStream()) {
          using (var deflateStream = new DeflateStream(memoryStream, CompressionMode.Compress)) {
            var writer = new StreamWriter(deflateStream);
            writer.Write(input);
            writer.Flush();
            compressedData = memoryStream.ToArray();
          }
        }
        break;
      default:
        throw new NotImplementedException($"Compression algorithm '{compressionAlgorithm}' is not supported");
    }

    // Encrypt the compressed data using the specified key
    byte[] encryptedData;
    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(encryptionKey)) {
      using (var aes = new AesManaged()) {
        aes.KeySize = 256;
        aes.BlockSize = 128;
        aes.Padding = PaddingMode.PKCS7;
        aes.Mode = CipherMode.CBC;
        aes.Key = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(encryptionKey);
        using (var encryptor = aes.CreateEncryptor()) {
          encryptedData = encryptor.TransformFinalBlock(compressedData, 0, compressedData.Length);
        }
      }
    } else {
      encryptedData = compressedData;
    }

    // Send the encrypted data to the remote API endpoint
    string response;
    using (var client = new HttpClient()) {
      var request = new HttpRequestMessage(HttpMethod.Post, endpoint);
      request.Content = new ByteArrayContent(encryptedData);
      response = await client.SendAsync(request).ConfigureAwait(false);
    }

    // Decompress and decrypt the data received from the server
    byte[] decryptedData;
    switch (compressionAlgorithm) {
      case "GZIP":
        using (var memoryStream = new MemoryStream(encryptedData)) {
          using (var gzipStream = new GZipStream(memoryStream, CompressionMode.Decompress)) {
            decryptedData = new byte[gzipStream.Length];
            await gzipStream.ReadAsync(decryptedData, 0, decryptedData.Length).ConfigureAwait(false);
          }
        }
        break;
      case "Deflate":
        using (var memoryStream = new MemoryStream(encryptedData)) {
          using (var deflateStream = new DeflateStream(memoryStream, CompressionMode.Decompress)) {
            decryptedData = new byte[deflateStream.Length];
            await deflateStream.ReadAsync(decryptedData, 0, decryptedData.Length).ConfigureAwait(false);
          }
        }
        break;
      default:
        throw new NotImplementedException($"Compression algorithm '{compressionAlgorithm}' is not supported");
    }

    if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(encryptionKey)) {
      using (var aes = new AesManaged()) {
        aes.KeySize = 256;
        aes.BlockSize = 128;
        aes.Padding = PaddingMode.PKCS7;
        aes.Mode = CipherMode.CBC;
        aes.Key = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(encryptionKey);
        using (var decryptor = aes.CreateDecryptor()) {
          decryptedData = decryptor.TransformFinalBlock(decryptedData, 0, decryptedData.Length);
        }
      }
    }

    // Deserialize the JSON response from the server
    T result;
    using (var streamReader = new StreamReader(new MemoryStream(decryptedData))) {
      var jsonSerializer = new DataContractJsonSerializer(typeof(T));
      result = (T)jsonSerializer.ReadObject(streamReader.BaseStream);
    }

    return result;
  }
}

// Implement a caching mechanism that can handle both in-memory and disk-based caching to minimize the number of requests sent to the server and optimize memory usage.

private static ConcurrentDictionary<string, CacheEntry> cache = new ConcurrentDictionary<string, CacheEntry>();

public class CacheEntry {
  public byte[] Data { get; set; }
  public int ExpirationTime { get; set; }
}

public async Task<T> GetFromCacheAsync<T>(string key) where T : class {
  if (cache.TryGetValue(key, out CacheEntry cacheEntry)) {
    var now = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeSeconds();
    if (now < cacheEntry.ExpirationTime) {
      return DeserializeJson<T>(cacheEntry.Data);
    } else {
      cache.TryRemove(key, out _);
    }
  }

  var result = await SendApiRequestAsync<T>(key).ConfigureAwait(false);
  if (result != null) {
    cache[key] = new CacheEntry() { Data = SerializeJson(result), ExpirationTime = DateTimeOffset.UtcNow.ToUnixTimeSeconds() + cacheDurationInSeconds };
  }

  return result;
}

// Implement a mechanism for users to specify custom compression algorithms and encryption keys while supporting standard ones out-of-the-box.

private static Dictionary<string, CompressionAlgorithm> supportedCompressionAlgorithms = new Dictionary<string, CompressionAlgorithm>() {
  { "GZIP", CompressionAlgorithm.GZip },
  { "Deflate", CompressionAlgorithm.Deflate }
};

private static string GetCompressionAlgorithm(string algorithm) {
  if (supportedCompressionAlgorithms.ContainsKey(algorithm)) {
    return supportedCompressionAlgorithms[algorithm];
  } else {
    throw new NotImplementedException($"Compression algorithm '{algorithm}' is not supported");
  }
}

private static Dictionary<string, EncryptionAlgorithm> supportedEncryptionAlgorithms = new Dictionary<string, EncryptionAlgorithm>() {
  { "AES", EncryptionAlgorithm.Aes },
  { "RSA", EncryptionAlgorithm.Rsa }
};

private static string GetEncryptionAlgorithm(string algorithm) {
  if (supportedEncryptionAlgorithms.ContainsKey(algorithm)) {
    return supportedEncryptionAlgorithms[algorithm];
  } else {
    throw new NotImplementedException($"Encryption algorithm '{algorithm}' is not supported");
  }
}

// Implement a mechanism for users to specify custom cache expiration times.

private static int cacheDurationInSeconds = 60; // Default cache duration of 1 minute

public async Task<T> GetFromCacheAsync<T>(string key, int? cacheDuration) where T : class {
  if (cacheDuration != null && cacheDuration > 0) {
    return await SendApiRequestAsync<T>(key).ConfigureAwait(false);
  } else {
    return await GetFromCacheAsync<T>(key).ConfigureAwait(false);
  }
}

// Implement a mechanism for users to invalidate the cache.

public async Task InvalidateCacheAsync(string key) {
  if (cache.TryRemove(key, out CacheEntry cacheEntry)) {
    // Do something with the removed cache entry
  }
}

