The `add` method takes two parameters: `rxUeInfo` and `crcIndication`. It creates a new `NfaApiCrcIndicationPdu` object with the specified parameters and adds it to the array. It also updates the `rntiMap` to map the `Rnti` to the index of the newly added element in the array.

The `remove` method takes one parameter: `rnti`. It uses the `rntiMap` to find the index of the element with the specified `Rnti` in the array. If it is found, it removes the element from the array and updates the `rntiMap` accordingly. Otherwise, it throws an error.

The `updateCrcFlag` method takes two parameters: `rnti` and `newCrcFlag`. It uses the `rntiMap` to find the index of the element with the specified `Rnti` in the array. If it is found, it updates the `crcIndication` field of the corresponding `NfaApiCrcIndicationPdu` object with the new value of `newCrcFlag`. Otherwise, it throws an error.

The `mtx` variable is used to protect the array and `rntiMap` from concurrent access. The `std::lock_guard<std::mutex>` class is used to acquire a lock on the `mtx` mutex before modifying the array or `rntiMap`. This ensures that only one thread can modify the data structure at a time, and prevents race conditions from occurring.

