The above code shows a basic implementation of the CryptKeeper design pattern. The `handleLogin()`, `handleRegistration()` and `handleResetPassword()` functions are responsible for handling the requests from the user, validating the input, generating a random string and hashed password if it is valid and storing the generated password in the database. The `integrateWithExternalApi()` function is used to verify the strength of the generated password using an external API.

