* `filePath`: The path of the file to be loaded.
* `concurrentRequests`: The maximum number of concurrent requests to make when loading data from external sources or APIs.
* `retryAttempts`: The number of times to retry a failed request before giving up.
* `retryInterval`: The amount of time to wait between retries.

The `LoadDataAsync` method is the main entry point for loading and deserializing data from binary files. It uses a `StreamReader` to read the contents of the file, and then iterates through each record in the stream using a `while` loop. Each record is deserialized using the `DeserializeRecordAsync` method, which returns an instance of the deserialized object.

The `DeserializeRecordAsync` method uses Newtonsoft.Json to deserialize the JSON data into an instance of the deserialized object. If there is an error during deserialization, it throws a new exception with a descriptive message.

This implementation uses asynchronous programming patterns and locking mechanisms where necessary to ensure thread-safety and handle concurrent access without data corruption. It also includes rate limiting and retries mechanisms to handle external API failures gracefully, and implements robust error handling and logging mechanisms to manage potential deserialization issues, connectivity failures with external services, and handle different types of exceptions across multiple service boundaries.

