The function first allocates memory for the new state list using `malloc`. If this allocation fails, it prints an error message and returns `NULL`. Otherwise, it initializes the new state list by setting its `states` field to a newly allocated array of size `num_initial_states`, and its `size` field to `0`. It also sets the `next` field of the last state in the initial list to point to the new list if necessary.

