The `generateRandomSequence` method takes two template parameters: the minimum and maximum range of the random numbers to generate. It uses a `std::lock_guard` to ensure that only one thread can access the MT19937 instances at a time. If the minimum value is greater than the maximum value, it throws an `std::invalid_argument`.

The method first generates a random number within the specified range using each MT19937 instance in parallel. It then returns a vector of random numbers that are guaranteed to be within the specified range.

This implementation is optimized for scalability and maintainability, considering future enhancements and potential integration with other parts of a larger application. It uses a `std::mutex` and `std::condition_variable` to ensure thread-safe access to the MT19937 instances, and it uses a template parameter to support both integer and floating-point types.

