Distributed System for Real-time Sensor Data Ingestion
----------------------------------------------

The following is an example of a distributed system for ingesting real-time sensor data from multiple IoT devices over MQTT and HTTP protocols into a graph database. The system is designed to handle dynamic and fluctuating data rates, varying data formats, and potential network disruptions, ensuring minimal impact on overall system availability.
```java
public class DistributedSensorDataIngestion {
    private final Map<String, IoTDevice> devices; // map of IoT device IDs to their respective classes
    private final MQTTClient mqttClient; // MQTT client for subscribing to sensor data topics
    private final HTTPClient httpClient; // HTTP client for sending sensor data to the graph database
    private final GraphDatabase graphDatabase; // graph database instance for storing sensor data

    public DistributedSensorDataIngestion(List<IoTDevice> devices, MQTTClient mqttClient, HTTPClient httpClient, GraphDatabase graphDatabase) {
        this.devices = new HashMap<>();
        this.mqttClient = mqttClient;
        this.httpClient = httpClient;
        this.graphDatabase = graphDatabase;

        for (IoTDevice device : devices) {
            this.devices.put(device.getId(), device);
        }
    }

    public void start() throws Exception {
        // subscribe to MQTT topics and handle incoming data
        mqttClient.subscribeToTopics(this::handleIncomingData);

        // send HTTP requests to the graph database for storing sensor data
        httpClient.sendRequests(graphDatabase::storeSensorData);
    }

    private void handleIncomingData(String topic, byte[] message) {
        try {
            String deviceId = topic.split("/")[1];
            IoTDevice device = devices.get(deviceId);

            if (device == null) {
                // handle unknown devices
                return;
            }

            SensorData data = device.parseSensorData(message);
            graphDatabase.storeSensorData(data);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // handle parsing errors or other exceptions
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```
The `DistributedSensorDataIngestion` class manages multiple IoT devices and their respective sensor data topics. It uses an MQTT client to subscribe to these topics and handles incoming sensor data using a custom `handleIncomingData()` method. The HTTP client is used to send requests to the graph database for storing sensor data.
