The `Server` class has a constructor that takes an instance of `IConfiguration`, which is used to get the configuration for the server, such as the port number and listen address. The `WebInterface` class also has a constructor that takes an instance of `IConfiguration` and an instance of `Server`, which allows it to share the same configuration with the `Server` class.

The `Start()` method of the `Server` class starts the HTTP listener and listens for incoming requests. The `Start()` method of the `WebInterface` class also starts the HTTP listener, but it also handles requests from the web interface by calling the `HandleRequest()` method when a request is received. The `HandleRequest()` method gets the input and output file paths from the request and uses an instance of `AudioTranscoder` to transcode the audio file. It then gets the metadata from the transcoded file using an instance of `TagLib.File` and writes it to the response stream.

The `Server` class also has a `Stop()` method that stops the HTTP listener when the server is stopped. The `WebInterface` class also has a `Stop()` method that stops the HTTP listener when the web interface is stopped.

function updateUserPassword($userId, $newPassword, array $recentPasswords, \PDO $dbConnection, \AuthSystem $authSystem) {
    // Validate the new password against the defined criteria
    if (!$this->validateNewPassword($newPassword)) {
        return false;
    }

    // Check if the user exists in the database
    $user = $authSystem->getUserById($userId);
    if ($user === null) {
        throw new \Exception("User does not exist");
    }

    // Hash the password using a secure hashing algorithm (e.g., bcrypt)
    $hashedPassword = $this->hashPassword($newPassword);

    // Check if the hashed password is different from the previous ones
    if (!$this->checkForReusedPasswords($recentPasswords, $hashedPassword)) {
        return false;
    }

    // Update the user's password in the database
    try {
        $dbConnection->beginTransaction();
        $stmt = $dbConnection->prepare("UPDATE users SET password = :password WHERE id = :userId");
        $stmt->bindParam(':password', $hashedPassword);
        $stmt->bindParam(':userId', $userId);
        $stmt->execute();
        $dbConnection->commit();
    } catch (\PDOException $e) {
        $dbConnection->rollBack();
        throw new \Exception("Failed to update password in database", 0, $e);
    }

    return true;
}
