The method is designed for both synchronous and asynchronous execution of commands, allowing developers to choose the appropriate approach based on their requirements. It also supports transaction management, ensuring all operations within a transaction are either committed or rolled back atomically.

To prevent overwhelming the database server with concurrent connections, the method includes a throttling mechanism that limits the number of concurrent database connections. The method also provides detailed metrics and monitoring capabilities to track the performance and usage of the method, including execution time, success rates, and resource consumption.

