  }

  // Join all threads to wait for their completion
  for (int i = 0; i < numThreads; i++) {
    pthread_join(threads[i], NULL);
  }

  // Close the semaphore
  sem_close(sem);

  return 0;
}
```
This program uses a combination of functions to modify filenames based on their format, validate filenames according to naming rules specified in an external configuration file, and log all modifications made to filenames. It also implements a rate-limiting mechanism to prevent the program from processing too many files at once, which could overload the system.

The program first checks if the configuration file exists and loads it into memory. It then checks if the directory to process exists and creates a semaphore for rate limiting. After that, it searches for files in the directory using a combination of `findFiles()` and `regexMatches()`. For each file found, it creates a new thread to modify it based on its format using `pthread_create()`.

The program then joins all threads to wait for their completion using `pthread_join()`. Finally, it closes the semaphore and returns 0.

You can compile this program with the following command:
```bash
gcc -o modify_file modify_file.c -lpthread -lrt
```
