import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import org.springframework.http.HttpStatus;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;
import org.springframework.web.server.ResponseStatusException;

@SpringBootApplication
public class PokemonService {
    @Autowired
    private ObjectMapper objectMapper;
    @Autowired
    private JedisPool jedisPool;
    @Autowired
    private ExecutorService executorService;

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(PokemonService.class, args);
    }

    @Bean
    public ObjectMapper objectMapper() {
        return new ObjectMapper();
    }

    @Bean
    public JedisPool jedisPool() {
        return new JedisPool("localhost");
    }

    @Bean
    public ExecutorService executorService() {
        return Executors.newCachedThreadPool();
    }

    @Service
    public class PokemonProcessor {
        private static final String CACHE_KEY_PREFIX = "pokemon_weaknesses";

        public List<String> getWeaknesses(byte[] pokemonBytes) throws JedisException, IOException {
            String pokemonType = objectMapper.readValue(pokemonBytes, Pokemon.class).getType();
            String cacheKey = CACHE_KEY_PREFIX + "_" + pokemonType;

            // Check if weaknesses are available in the cache
            if (jedisPool.exists(cacheKey)) {
                return jedisPool.get(cacheKey);
            } else {
                // Fetch weaknesses from external API and store in cache
                String apiResponse = getWeaknessesFromApi(pokemonType);
                jedisPool.set(cacheKey, apiResponse);
                return objectMapper.readValue(apiResponse, List.class);
            }
        }

        public String getWeaknessesFromApi(String pokemonType) throws IOException {
            // Make API call to retrieve weaknesses for the given Pokémon type
            ResponseEntity<String> response = restTemplate.exchange("https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon/" + pokemonType + "/weaknesses", HttpMethod.GET, null, String.class);
            if (response.getStatusCode() == HttpStatus.OK) {
                return response.getBody();
            } else {
                throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST, "Unable to retrieve weaknesses for " + pokemonType);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
This code defines a Spring Boot application that includes a `PokemonProcessor` class that handles the business logic of retrieving weaknesses for different Pokémon types. The `PokemonProcessor` uses Redis as a distributed caching mechanism to store frequently accessed Pokémon types and their weaknesses locally, reducing latency. For less common types, it fetches additional data from an external REST API.

The `PokemonService` class is the entry point of the application and includes several beans that are used to configure the service:

* `objectMapper()`: The `ObjectMapper` bean is used to convert between JSON and Java objects.
* `jedisPool()`: The `JedisPool` bean is used to manage connections to Redis.
* `executorService()`: The `ExecutorService` bean is used to handle concurrent deserialization tasks.

The `PokemonProcessor` class implements the business logic of retrieving weaknesses for different Pokémon types. It uses Redis as a distributed caching mechanism to store frequently accessed Pokémon types and their weaknesses locally, reducing latency. For less common types, it fetches additional data from an external REST API using Spring's `RestTemplate`.

The service is designed to provide real-time feedback on the status of incoming streams, including throughput and error rates, to improve user experience and usability. It also includes robust error handling to manage failures in deserialization, network issues, and unavailable API responses, providing clear and actionable error messages.

The service is able to operate in both offline and online modes, where in offline mode it uses a local database for all Pokémon type information and does not make API calls, and in online mode it integrates with the external REST API for additional data.

