In this code, we use a lambda expression to define the comparison function object. The lambda expression takes two arguments `a` and `b`, which are both of type `string`. It returns `true` if `a == b` or if the first character of `a` is equal to the first character of `b`.

By using a case-insensitive comparison, we can search for elements in the map using a different case than the one used when inserting them. This can be useful in cases where the user enters data with mixed case or uses different case conventions.

