The code first checks if the file exists and can be read using `Files.readAllBytes()`. If it does not exist or cannot be read, it throws an `IOException`.

Next, it generates a random key of length 16 bytes (AES-128) using `SecureRandom`. It then initializes the cipher instance and returns an `EVP_CIPHER` object. The `EVP_CIPHER` object is used to encrypt the file contents using the `encrypt()` method of the OpenSSL library.

The `encryptFile()` method also computes the MD5 hash of the file contents before encryption, and returns it as part of the encrypted content. This allows the decryption code to verify that the decrypted contents match the original file contents.

