The code uses a `Mutex` to synchronize access to the map of clinics, preventing concurrent modifications to the same entry while allowing other entries to be accessed simultaneously. It also uses `reqwest` to fetch the remote address of the request and `chrono` to manage dates and times. The `Error` struct is defined to represent error cases with a reason string that can be used for debugging purposes.

To validate the clinic ID, it checks if the ID exists in the map of clinics using the `contains_key()` method. If not found, it returns an `InvalidId` error with a user-friendly message. Otherwise, it updates the corresponding clinic with the new status and last modified IP address, and returns a success message.

To handle retries for failed requests and backoff strategies, you can add a retry mechanism to the `update_status()` function that uses an exponential backoff algorithm to wait for increasing amounts of time between retries. You can also use a circuit breaker pattern to prevent too many retries if the external API is down or not responding.

