The `ConvertToDataTable` method is not implemented here as it depends on your specific data conversion logic. However, you can use any third-party library or write your own code to convert JSON strings to `DataTable` objects.

The caching mechanism uses a simple JSON file-based storage system that stores cached queries with their corresponding result sets. The `IsCachedQuery` method checks if the query is already cached in memory or on disk, and the `CacheQuery` method writes the cached data to a JSON file. The `GetCachedDataTable` method reads the cached data from a JSON file and returns it as a `DataTableReader`.

The caching mechanism also supports configuring cache expiration time using the `cacheExpirationTime` parameter in the constructor. If the cache is enabled, it will check if the query is already cached before performing a new request to the server. This can help reduce the number of requests sent to the server and improve performance by reducing the need for repeated queries.

The method also includes a retry mechanism using an exponential backoff algorithm with jitter to handle failed transmissions. This ensures that the system can adapt to varying network conditions and provides robustness against temporary failures. The `throttling` mechanism is not implemented here but you can use any third-party library or write your own code to limit the rate at which data is copied to prevent overwhelming the system.

