The `main` function loads the configuration file and sets up the backend service details, connection pool, and event-driven message broker. It then creates a thread pool for handling API requests, which are processed asynchronously using the `post` method of the `thread_pool` object. The `handleRequest` function validates incoming requests, loads the backend service details from the configuration file, and handles the request based on its type (GET_PRODUCTS, ADD_TO_CART, or CHECKOUT).

