This code creates a semaphore with the specified initial value, and then processes all the log files in the current directory using the `readdir()` function. It splits each line into timestamp, IP address, and request method, and stores the data in a structure for further processing. The program calculates and prints the average number of requests per minute for each log file, handling file rotation and efficiently managing memory to avoid loading all log data into memory at once. Robust error handling is implemented to deal with missing files, permission issues, and malformed log entries. The program uses standard library functions for semaphore operations and is structured to allow for modular development, where the C part handles semaphore management and the Python part handles log file processing.

