The `exec()` function is used to execute shell commands asynchronously and handle any errors that may occur during the conversion process. It uses the `io_service` class from Boost::Asio to create an asynchronous IO service, which allows for parallel processing of multiple requests without blocking the main thread. The function then gets the response from the server and handles any errors that may occur during the conversion process.

The `getPdfFilePath()` function is used to get the PDF file path for an image file based on its input directory and output directory parameters. The function first finds the last occurrence of a period in the image file name (assuming it is a filename without an extension) and then appends the ".pdf" extension to the file name to create the PDF file path.

