The code also includes a deadlock detection and mitigation feature, which prevents potential issues in the thread pool by checking if any threads are stuck in an infinite loop. It also implements comprehensive error handling mechanisms to handle invalid input parameters, version mismatches, and I/O errors.

Additionally, the code includes a configurable rate limiter to control the number of PDUs generated per second based on network conditions and system load. The rate limiter can be used to adjust the number of threads in the thread pool based on the current system load to ensure efficient use of computational resources.

