In this example, we have implemented a `ProductService` class that provides methods for retrieving product information from an external API. We have also added some additional functionality such as caching of product information to improve performance, as well as the ability to predict future inventory status based on historical sales data.

The service uses Java 8's built-in `CompletableFuture` class to handle asynchronous calls to the API endpoints and return a `Future` object that can be used to retrieve the results at a later time. This allows us to perform multiple API requests in parallel and process their results as they become available, without blocking on individual requests.

The service also includes error handling to gracefully handle any exceptions that may occur during API calls. Instead of crashing the application, these errors can be handled and logged, allowing the service to continue functioning normally.

In addition to this, we have also implemented a mechanism for retrieving historical product information from an external API and caching it in-memory. This allows us to retrieve product information from an external source without having to make multiple API requests each time the application starts up.

Finally, we have added the ability to retrieve recommended products based on user browsing history and purchase behavior. This allows us to provide users with personalized product recommendations that they may not have tried yet.

