```java
package com.example.service;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;

public class SerializationService {
    private static final Map<Class<?>, Deserializer<?>> deserializers = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    public static <T> T deserialize(byte[] bytes, Class<T> clazz) throws DeserializationException {
        try {
            // Check if the class has a registered deserializer
            Deserializer<T> deserializer = (Deserializer<T>) deserializers.get(clazz);
            if (deserializer == null) {
                // If not, create one and register it
                deserializer = new Deserializer<>(clazz);
                deserializers.put(clazz, deserializer);
            }

            // Deserialize the object using the registered deserializer
            return deserializer.deserialize(bytes);
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            throw new DeserializationException("Failed to deserialize object", e);
        }
    }

    public static void registerDeserializer(Class<?> clazz, Deserializer<?> deserializer) {
        deserializers.put(clazz, deserializer);
    }

    private static class Deserializer<T> {
        private final Class<T> clazz;

        public Deserializer(Class<T> clazz) {
            this.clazz = clazz;
        }

        public T deserialize(byte[] bytes) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
            try (ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(new ByteArrayInputStream(bytes))) {
                return clazz.cast(ois.readObject());
            }
        }
    }
}
```
Configuration and setup guide:

1. Configure the distributed file system to use a specific directory or location for storing serialized objects.
2. Create a cache system, such as a hash map, to store deserialized objects in memory.
3. Register the deserializers for each class that needs to be handled by the service.
4. Implement the error handling mechanism by throwing a custom `DeserializationException` with detailed information when deserialization fails.
5. Optimize the service for performance in a high-concurrency environment by managing resources efficiently and closing all I/O streams properly.
6. Ensure the service can scale to handle large numbers of objects and concurrent requests by using a robust caching strategy, such as LRU or least recently used.
7. Provide comprehensive unit and integration tests to validate the service's functionality, error handling, and performance under stress conditions.

Example usage:
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        // Register deserializers for classes that need to be handled by the service
        SerializationService.registerDeserializer(MyClass1.class, new MyClass1Deserializer());
        SerializationService.registerDeserializer(MyClass2.class, new MyClass2Deserializer());

        // Read serialized bytes from a distributed file system
        byte[] bytes = readSerializedBytesFromFileSystem();

        // Deserialize the object using the registered deserializer
        MyClass1 myObject1 = SerializationService.deserialize(bytes, MyClass1.class);
        MyClass2 myObject2 = SerializationService.deserialize(bytes, MyClass2.class);
    }
}
