This service will provide a simple interface to access and manipulate the data in the pokemon database. It will expose three endpoints:

* `/pokemons`: This endpoint will return all the pokemons in the database.
* `/pokemons/{name}`: This endpoint will return the details of a specific pokemon based on its name.
* `/update`: This endpoint will update the data in the pokemon database by reading a JSON file and updating the existing records.

### Data Model

The data model for this service will be a simple one, with each pokemon having three properties: `name`, `type`, and `description`. The `name` property will be unique, and the `type` property will be an enum of `grass`, `fire`, `water`, `electric`, `normal`, or `poison`. The `description` property will be a brief summary of the pokemon.

Here is an example of what the data model might look like:
```json
