This deployment strategy uses a Kubernetes deployment to run the service with multiple replicas. The `replicas` field is set to 2, which means that there will be two instances of the service running at all times. The `ports` field specifies that the container should listen on port 8080 and map it to port 80 on the host. The `selector` field specifies that the deployment should select pods with a label `app: pokemon-service`.

The service is then exposed through a Kubernetes service, which allows clients to access the service using its ClusterIP address. In this example, the service is exposed on port 80 of the host.

